      "math_academy_id": "e-1749",
      "problem": "For the function $g(x)$ defined on the set of integers, find $g(-12)$ and $g(3),$ where $g(x)$ is the following piecewise function:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192535/assets/acfad4c4a64718b1a2915719ede798e3b78109061ffd8cf88f6c3acd38920eae.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "- First, we compute $g(-12).$ Since $-12 < 1,$ we use the first branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =2x \\\\ g(-12) & =2(-12) \\\\  & =-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we compute $g(3).$ Since $3 \\geq 1,$ we use the second branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =3x \\\\ g(3) & =3(3) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
